    "content": {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Signed-change situations"
        },
        {
          "type": "subheading",
          "text": "A story about temperature"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The temperature at 7:00 AM was -7 degrees C. By noon it rose by 8 degrees. The change is +8. Add: -7 + 8 = 1. The new temperature is 1 degree C."
        },
        {
          "type": "subheading",
          "text": "Words that mean signs"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Rise, gain, deposit, and up mean positive changes. Fall, loss, withdrawal, and down mean negative changes."
        },
        {
          "type": "subheading",
          "text": "Interpreting the result"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Always include the unit. Say if the result is positive or negative. Explain what it means."
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "image_asset": "lesson/lesson-3/temperature-change.png",
          "image_alt": "Number line showing start at -7 and endpoint at 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "worked_example",
          "title": "Modeling a change",
          "problem": "A diver is at -12 m and rises 5 m. Where is the diver now?",
          "steps": [
            "Step 1: The start is -12. Rises means a positive change: +5.",
            "Step 2: Add: -12 + 5 = -7.",
            "Step 3: Interpret: the diver is 7 m below sea level."
          ],
          "answer": "-7 m (7 m below sea level)"
        },
        {
          "type": "common_mistake",
          "text": "Writing a fall of 6 degrees as +6 is wrong. Fall means a negative change, so write -6."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "cta",
          "text": "Ready to practice. Continue to the regular exercise for 6 questions."
        }
      ],
      "source_text": "Lesson 3.2 - Signed-change situations\nSkill: S6\nObjective:\n1. Model signed-change situations.\nA story about temperature\nThe temperature at 7:00 AM was -7 degrees C. By noon it rose by 8 degrees.\nThe change is +8. Add: -7 + 8 = 1.\nThe new temperature is 1 degree C.\nWords that mean signs\nRise, gain, deposit, up -> positive.\nFall, loss, withdrawal, down -> negative.\nInterpreting the result\nAlways include the unit. Say if the result is positive or negative. Explain what it means.\nWorked example\nProblem: A diver is at -12 m and rises 5 m. Where is the diver now?\nStep 1: The start is -12. Rises means a positive change: +5.\nStep 2: Add: -12 + 5 = -7.\nStep 3: Interpret: the diver is 7 m below sea level.\nAnswer: -7 m (7 m below sea level).\nCommon mistake\nWriting a fall of 6 degrees as +6 is wrong. Fall means a negative change, so write -6."
    }
  },
